     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg. I don't know of any indication that supports it. Above those doses, analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau and the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events keeps rising. This is a patient-safety limit, so I'm not treating it as a routine confirmation.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** Examples are 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 800 mg PO three times daily. I can enter either now.\n- **Add a scheduled adjunct if pain control is the goal.** Acetaminophen is one option, and I can enter that too.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending first.** If you think there's a real reason to go above the maximum, they can review it. The order can then go in through whatever override or approval process your hospital requires.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
